As a user, I would like links to the relevant CLL page (or other webpage) t=
hat explains each word in context with its grammatical category.* (For me, =
the smaller "grammar words" are a higher priority than gismu etc.)


For example, the jbovlaste description of "pu" or "zi" really only makes an=
y sense if one has already read http://www.lojban.org/publications/referenc=
e_grammar/chapter10.html


I'm struggling trying to read real-world Lojban text because I can't unders=
tand the grammatical constructs that aren't explained well on jbovlaste. It=
's too difficult for me to read through the entire CLL (and I've been disco=
uraged by it being out-of-date) front-to-back.

Jbovlaste needs "on-demand" learning like this - to me, that's what a dicti=
onary is for.


*Alternatively, just insert the explanation directly, but I think inserting=
 the link should be easy to begin with.

